Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 39 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   95    WITH A MUCINOUS COMPONENT  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   EXTENDING TO LESS THAN 1 HIGH POWER FIELD FROM THE DEEP MARGIN AND AN ADDITIONAL MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   5    LOW GRADE  3  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  ALL 8 LYMPH NODES DISPLAY PROMINENT EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  4  MONCKEBERG S MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progestrogne receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast tissue  is a left modified radical mastectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm skin ellipse containing a central 2 5cm unremarkable nipple  No definite scar is identified  Attached to the specimen is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm  stellate tan mass that focally extends to within less than 1 0mm of the deep resection margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Section Code  A  mass with deep resection margin  representative section  B E  mass  representative sections  F  nipple trisected in entirety  G  unremarkable parenchyma  representative sections  The axillary tail is sectioned to reveal a 2 5cm focus of matted lymph nodes with a homogenous tan cut surface  Further sectioning reveals several firm lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  All have a homogeneous tan cut surface  Representative sections of the lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes H through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
