Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 12 45 CLINICAL DATA  Patient with calcifications on the left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  SEE TABLE  1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Involving 10 of 12 blocks  Grade  1  Calcifications  Limited to benign changes  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 2cm from the margin of the specimen in several foci  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 00                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm white tan fibrofatty breast tissue  There are three wires present in the specimen labeled anterior  posterior and middle  The anterior and posterior wires are loosely attached to the tissue and easily removed  The remaining metal wire is removed  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a white tan cut surface comprising   20  of the area and yellow adipose tissue  There are multiple scattered 0 5cm and less cystic spaces  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A L  Resident  CHAD SOUPIR  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Moderate_(grade_II).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  DURAY  PAUL  HARRISON  M D   DIAGNOSIS  by DURAY PAUL HARRISON M D   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   Fibrocystic change  focally proliferative   Microcalcifications are present in association with benign breast tissue   Scattered  multi centric secretory hyperplasia  duct micropapillation and  proliferative effect   NOTE  This is an unusual and interesting spectrum of duct epithelial secretory  effect that while proliferative  suggests a physiologic response   perhaps as a  drug effect  These changes may be accounting for the nipple discharge   Case seen also by Dr  Susan Lester   SURGICAL ADDENDUM  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D   This case was reviewed by Dr  James Connolly and Dr  Susan Lester by request   As stated in the original report  multiple ducts and lobules throughout the  specimen  in ten of ten slides  are filled with a population of cells with an  unusual secretory appearance  The cells have abundant vacuolated cytoplasm and  apocrine snouts  Some lumina are filled with eosinophilic secretory material   often associated with secretory calcifications  The nuclei are enlarged with  prominent nucleoli and some pleomorphism  The involved areas extend to within  0 1cm of the margin in multiple slides   Given the extent of the lesion and the atypia of the nuclei  it is felt that  this lesion most likely represents an unusual type of DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  with secretory features  This type of DCIS is very rare and has not been  described well in the literature  Tavassoli  F  Pathology of the Breast   REMOVED_CASE_ID     CLINICAL DATA   History  None given   TISSUE SUBMITTED  Mass right breast   O R  CONSULTATION   MASS RIGHT BREAST   No areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma   Gross examination only   RADIOLOGY  Calcifications seen in specimen radiograph   T  FRENNA M D  GROSS 