alue of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast biopsy  are two fragments of soft tissue  one is a fragment of breast REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The other is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse  The breast fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal mottled  white tan  fatty tissue  The skin fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm white  tan firm tissue beneath the epidermis  Representative sections from both fragments are frozen in FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the breast tissue is submitted entirely in cassette B  The remainder of the skin fragment are submitted entirely in cassettes C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a 640 gram  20 x 15 x 4 2cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 20 x 15cm skin ellipse in front with a 3cm horizontal incision closed with sutures just medial to the nipple  Attached axillary tail measures 10 x 6 x 2 0cm  The entire specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm irregularly shaped white firm mass that grossly abuts against the posterior resection margin on the medial half of the specimen  SECTION CODE D  Tumor mass at posterior margin  medial half  E  Medial end of the tumor  F  Section taken from the middle of the tumor  G  Section of tumor at its lateral end  Thirteen lymph nodes of varying sizes are dissected from the axi