Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Aleksandr Vasilyev  M D  Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D             Revised Report            Reason for Amendment  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Excision of DCIS  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT 12 30   EXCISION  1  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL   SEE NOTE   2  BACKGROUND OF FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  APOCRINE CYSTS AND ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  3  MYXOID FIBROADENOMAS  0 5 AND REMOVED_DATE CM   NOTE  Multiple levels were examined   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  see gross description  An E cadherin stain   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   shows the ductal and lobular epithelium to be consistently positive  which does not support the presence of lobular neoplasia  Dr  F  Koerner has reviewed selected slides and concurs  BREAST  LEFT LOWER OUTER QUADRANT   EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH COMEDONECROSIS AND CALCIFICATIONS   SEE TABLE    SEE NOTE   2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH APOCRINE CYSTS AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Scattered microscopic foci  involving 4 of 10 blocks and spanning at least 1 1cm  GRADE  3  CALCIFICATIONS  Limited to the carcinoma in situ  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to the inked margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Not indicated  see prior report from core biopsy  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Few foci are suspicious for microinvasion on the HE slides  However  microinvasion could not be definitively confirmed by immunohistochemical stains for myoepithelial cells  p63  calponin  myosin heavy chain  and cytokeratin  which show the ductal carcinoma in situ to be accompanied by myoepithelial cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    An E cadherin stain   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   shows the ductal and lobular epithelium to be consistently positive  which does not support the presence of lobular neoplasia  Dr  F  Koerner has reviewed selected slides and concurs  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast 12 30 position   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm lumpectomy specimen with a short suture indicating anterior  a long suture indicating lateral and bowtie indicating cephalad  There is a guide wire entering anterolaterally  The anterior is inked blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a few blue domed cysts and few areas of slight hemorrhage  The specimen is submitted representatively as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  including the medial margin  enface in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the lateral margin  enface in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy outer quadrant   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch indicating anterior  long stitch indicating lateral and bowtie indicating cephalad  There are two guide wires entering inferiorly  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two areas of hemorrhage correlating to the locations of the guide wire  The middle portion of the specimen appears bulkier with less fat but no discrete lesions are aside from a few blue domed cysts present throughout the specimen  The specimen is serially sectioned and representatively submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  including the medial margin  enface in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the lateral margin  enface in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The area between the two hemorrhagic foci is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and tissues lateral to the lateral guide wire in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT 12 30   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT LOWER OUTER QUADRANT   EXCISION , Moderate_(grade_II).
