Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal right mammography prior left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  INVOLVING A NODULE COMPOSED OF GLANDS AND STROMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The classification of this lesion is unclear  The stromal proliferation probably represents pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia  The stromal proliferation might recur locally  The atypical ductal hyperplasia might represent a reactive phenomenon  but the possibility of a preneoplastic proliferation cannot be excluded  The atypical ductal hyperplasia does not involve the tissue adjacent to the nodule  The cells of the lobular neoplasia stain for keratin 903 but fail to stain for e cadherin  The lobular neoplasia extends into tissue adjacent to the nodule  The lesion does not resemble the fibroadenoma resected from the patient s right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 03                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy  is an unoriented  round  2 5cm in diameter fibroadipose tissue specimen with a localization wire in place  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes A D with ends in A  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Lela Polivogianis  M D  PART 